Fake cops, man.

4305
04:30:59,330 --> 04:31:04,790
Driscoll explained that he found watching pornography very calming during car chases, but that the video had frozen.

4306
04:31:05,190 --> 04:31:06,310
It was so frustrating.

4307
04:31:06,650 --> 04:31:10,330
The dude had walked in on his hot stepmom having a shower, and then nothing.

4308
04:31:10,650 --> 04:31:15,110
I was trying to refresh the stupid video, and boom, I'm upside down and there's smoke everywhere.

4309
04:31:15,450 --> 04:31:17,830
I think Booty Bang owes everyone a big apology.

4310
04:31:18,370 --> 04:31:19,530
Come on, guys, do better.

4311
04:31:20,250 --> 04:31:21,170
And you know what?

4312
04:31:21,450 --> 04:31:24,650
He probably even got a raise after that.

4313
04:31:29,170 --> 04:31:29,730
Yeah.

4314
04:31:29,730 --> 04:31:31,430
Alright, let's actually go to bed.

4315
04:31:32,310 --> 04:31:33,650
It's six in the morning.

4316
04:31:34,910 --> 04:31:36,510
Sleep until noon.

4317
04:31:38,410 --> 04:31:39,370
That sounds right.

4318
04:31:47,800 --> 04:31:48,460
Get dressed.

4319
04:31:49,020 --> 04:31:50,420
What happens if I click that?

4320
04:31:50,580 --> 04:31:51,800
Okay, I should immediately get dressed.

4321
04:31:51,980 --> 04:31:52,040
Okay.

4322
04:31:53,040 --> 04:31:53,300
Sweet.

4323
04:31:54,140 --> 04:31:55,520
I guess we skipped the shower today.

4324
04:31:55,700 --> 04:31:56,000
You know what?

4325
04:31:56,120 --> 04:31:57,120
That's actually a good idea.

4326
04:31:58,260 --> 04:31:59,360
Workout window opens.

4327
04:31:59,760 --> 04:32:01,420
We're gonna get a workout a different way today.

4328
04:32:03,240 --> 04:32:04,860
I don't know how often you should feed a snake.

4329
04:32:05,000 --> 04:32:07,820
I guess tonight I'll feed that snake again.

4330
04:32:08,620 --> 04:32:09,620
Let's go do some painting.

4331
04:32:13,710 --> 04:32:15,550
Some chores around the house.

4332
04:32:16,870 --> 04:32:20,690
Stormy blue paint or tropical green paint?

4333
04:32:21,770 --> 04:32:22,350
Hmm.

4334
04:32:23,830 --> 04:32:24,530
Stormy.

4335
04:32:26,230 --> 04:32:26,990
Definitely.

4336
04:32:36,770 --> 04:32:37,530
Yes.

4337
04:32:38,290 --> 04:32:39,210
Come on, Jason.

4338
04:32:39,750 --> 04:32:40,750
Oh, I gotta do it.

4339
04:32:40,830 --> 04:32:41,150
Okay, okay.

4340
04:32:41,350 --> 04:32:41,730
I'm down.

4341
04:32:49,140 --> 04:32:49,660
Nice.

4342
04:32:49,660 --> 04:32:50,940
Ooh, I love that sound.

4343
04:32:53,260 --> 04:32:53,780
Yes.

4344
04:32:56,260 --> 04:32:57,700
GTA 6, people.

4345
04:32:59,780 --> 04:33:00,760
And I love it.

4346
04:33:07,700 --> 04:33:08,940
This guy is brave, though.

4347
04:33:10,080 --> 04:33:11,880
No protection at all on the floor.

4348
04:33:15,610 --> 04:33:16,630
I guess he's just confident.

4349
04:33:19,970 --> 04:33:20,970
What about the roof, though?

4350
04:33:21,110 --> 04:33:22,750
Like, why did you leave such a gap down there?

4351
04:33:26,490 --> 04:33:27,870
Okay, he's kind of doing it, I guess.

4352
04:33:29,930 --> 04:33:31,670
Okay, how are you going to handle that outlet, though?

4353
04:33:31,890 --> 04:33:32,650
Let me see the skills.

4354
04:33:33,830 --> 04:33:35,390
You got to put some tape around that, brother.

4355
04:33:40,330 --> 04:33:41,190
Oh, here it goes.

4356
04:33:41,310 --> 04:33:44,330
Is he gonna... Oh, they don't even show that.

4357
04:33:45,550 --> 04:33:46,770
I needed to see his technique.

4358
04:33:47,030 --> 04:33:48,270
Okay, wait a minute.

4359
04:33:48,410 --> 04:33:49,770
This is not the blue I was imagining.

4360
04:33:51,590 --> 04:33:52,710
That's more like turquoise.

4361
04:33:55,090 --> 04:33:56,230
That's right, I know my colors.

4362
04:34:00,060 --> 04:34:01,420
I gotta figure out how to fish.

4363
04:34:02,020 --> 04:34:05,300
But maybe we should... Oh, wait a minute.

4364
04:34:05,560 --> 04:34:06,780
We need to fix the roof as well.

4365
04:34:08,220 --> 04:34:09,100
We ain't done here.

4366
04:34:10,380 --> 04:34:10,780
Whoa!

4367
04:34:16,320 --> 04:34:17,160
There's a bird up there.

4368
04:34:19,380 --> 04:34:19,780
Inspect?

4369
04:34:25,480 --> 04:34:25,920
What?

4370
04:34:27,820 --> 04:34:28,260
Oh.

4371
04:34:29,120 --> 04:34:31,180
Wait, you can actually just zoom in on things?

4372
04:34:34,340 --> 04:34:35,560
Or was that... No?

4373
04:34:35,900 --> 04:34:39,100
When I stand like this, I can... Oh, it's this button.

4374
04:34:39,840 --> 04:34:41,160
Oh, that's so nice!

4375
04:34:41,540 --> 04:34:42,640
I have to remember this.

4376
04:34:43,600 --> 04:34:47,200
You can go into a sort of semi-first-person mode there.

4377
04:34:47,580 --> 04:34:48,520
Just to look around.

4378
04:34:48,660 --> 04:34:49,040
That's neat.

4379
04:34:55,300 --> 04:34:56,080
All right, Jason.

4380
04:34:58,100 --> 04:34:59,320
Are we done with the roof here?

4381
04:35:01,500 --> 04:35:02,720
We were done with the roof.

4382
04:35:03,040 --> 04:35:03,560
Let me see what it said.

4383
04:35:08,040 --> 04:35:09,740
Oh, railing and steps.

4384
04:35:11,040 --> 04:35:14,060
Railing is the thing on the landing here, isn't it?

4385
04:35:16,580 --> 04:35:18,240
I guess we've got to find the spot that's broken.

4386
04:35:23,700 --> 04:35:24,680
And we're back here.

4387
04:35:34,500 --> 04:35:36,280
Do we see a railing that's broken?

4388
04:35:39,920 --> 04:35:40,660
What is that?

4389
04:35:46,210 --> 04:35:47,090
Is that a brick?

4390
04:35:47,250 --> 04:35:47,910
Oh, wait a minute.

4391
04:35:47,990 --> 04:35:51,730
It's the thing that you use to smoothen the edges on wood.

4392
04:35:54,210 --> 04:35:55,030
Oh, here we go.

4393
04:36:00,290 --> 04:36:01,150
There it is.

4394
04:36:02,950 --> 04:36:04,890
Yeah, it just has that line next to him.

4395
04:36:05,610 --> 04:36:06,330
Ready to go.

4396
04:36:16,570 --> 04:36:19,750
Like, I wouldn't mind a whole game just with this, you know?

4397
04:36:19,870 --> 04:36:20,470
Home restoration.

4398
04:36:21,630 --> 04:36:22,610
Sign me up, man.

4399
04:36:24,470 --> 04:36:26,050
I don't care about shooting people.

4400
04:36:26,310 --> 04:36:27,350
Let me fix my home.

4401
04:36:31,510 --> 04:36:32,510
Okay, so that's done.

4402
04:36:32,890 --> 04:36:33,330
Wonderful.

4403
04:36:39,160 --> 04:36:42,440
And the last one, I think, is actually back here.

4404
04:36:44,940 --> 04:36:46,600
So much character to this home.

4405
04:36:47,500 --> 04:36:48,160
Isn't there?

4406
04:36:50,160 --> 04:36:51,900
I want a place like this so bad.

4407
04:36:53,680 --> 04:36:54,880
I think we're just down here.

4408
04:36:55,180 --> 04:36:55,840
Fix the steps.

4409
04:36:58,620 --> 04:36:59,580
Ah, here we go.

4410
04:37:07,270 --> 04:37:10,450
Oh wait, they're old and need replacing maybe.

4411
04:37:12,390 --> 04:37:13,110
Come on.

4412
04:37:13,450 --> 04:37:14,250
There we go.

4413
04:37:16,110 --> 04:37:18,390
All that workout is paying off here.

4414
04:37:24,910 --> 04:37:25,470
Sweet.

4415
04:37:28,550 --> 04:37:32,210
I love that they put so much emphasis on these little things here.

4416
04:37:33,610 --> 04:37:36,550
That actually is very promising for the rest of the game for me.

4417
04:37:38,610 --> 04:37:40,670
This is exactly my type of jam, you know?

4418
04:37:46,950 --> 04:37:47,470
Wonderful.

4419
04:37:53,130 --> 04:37:56,030
The last one.

4420
04:38:01,560 --> 04:38:03,020
I'm a pro with this thing now.

4421
04:38:07,940 --> 04:38:08,380
Yeah.

4422
04:38:10,340 --> 04:38:10,780
Alright.

4423
04:38:11,880 --> 04:38:13,200
House repairs complete.

4424
04:38:15,280 --> 04:38:16,120
That feels good.

4425
04:38:20,920 --> 04:38:21,840
Let's get in the car.

4426
04:38:22,020 --> 04:38:23,260
Hey, let's see if my bike is here.

4427
04:38:23,860 --> 04:38:25,140
Did it actually return?

4428
04:38:25,680 --> 04:38:26,840
It did return.

4429
04:38:27,060 --> 04:38:27,320
Okay.

4430
04:38:27,640 --> 04:38:29,560
So we don't have to worry about picking the bike up.

4431
04:38:33,760 --> 04:38:34,340
Let's go.

4432
04:38:36,500 --> 04:38:36,940
Now.

4433
04:38:38,580 --> 04:38:39,460
Where are we going?

4434
04:38:41,520 --> 04:38:42,960
Why is there a marker right there?

4435
04:38:44,460 --> 04:38:45,100
Remove that.

4436
04:38:46,660 --> 04:38:49,380
I think next up we should do maybe that one.

4437
04:38:50,080 --> 04:38:51,160
Collect Brian's rent.

4438
04:38:51,300 --> 04:38:52,880
It's been a while since we got this mission.

4439
04:38:54,780 --> 04:38:55,740
Let's get down there.

4440
04:38:59,690 --> 04:39:04,650
There's also this weird thing in the shop with the birds that we could check out.

4441
04:39:42,860 --> 04:39:45,760
Ha ha ha.

4442
04:40:01,900 --> 04:40:05,260
I have never seen anyone in real life on a scooter like that.

4443
04:40:05,740 --> 04:40:06,120
Never.

4444
04:40:07,540 --> 04:40:11,280
I don't even know if that's a real thing in America and people actually do that.

4445
04:40:11,420 --> 04:40:12,640
It seems crazy to me.

4446
04:40:14,320 --> 04:40:15,960
Like, what the fuck, man.

4447
04:40:21,460 --> 04:40:22,180
Alright, let's go.

4448
04:40:27,040 --> 04:40:27,660
Turn right.

4449
04:40:27,720 --> 04:40:29,580
I love that little indicator down there, man.

4450
04:40:33,510 --> 04:40:36,470
In fact, you could probably do without the minimap and just have that indicator.

4451
04:40:38,290 --> 04:40:40,470
Maybe you can actually do that if you turn off minimap.

4452
04:40:41,910 --> 04:40:44,010
I think I'll experiment with that at some point.

4453
04:40:44,970 --> 04:40:47,090
For now, though, I'm just learning the game.

4454
04:40:49,820 --> 04:40:50,720
Getting the basics.

4455
04:40:52,320 --> 04:40:56,440
God, it's funny how everything looks so different depending on the time of day.

4456
04:40:56,780 --> 04:40:59,640
This is almost not recognizable right now for me.

4457
04:41:00,880 --> 04:41:03,520
Because I've mostly been driving here at night and stuff, in dusk.

4458
04:41:10,160 --> 04:41:12,700
That looks like a money transport thingy.

4459
04:41:12,700 --> 04:41:16,840
I wonder if that's a thing in this game where you can rob vehicles like that.

4460
04:41:20,320 --> 04:41:20,980
That'd be dope.

4461
04:41:21,640 --> 04:41:23,220
Also, I need to take care of this car here.

4462
04:41:23,360 --> 04:41:25,920
It's looking hella clean right now, doesn't it?

4463
04:41:26,680 --> 04:41:27,820
We can't mess this up.

4464
04:41:31,500 --> 04:41:32,460
It's very important.

4465
04:41:34,960 --> 04:41:37,840
Okay, so we have to retrieve some money here for Brian.

4466
04:41:43,540 --> 04:41:44,560
People having arguments?

4467
04:41:55,470 --> 04:41:56,130
Wait a minute.

4468
04:41:56,470 --> 04:41:58,290
This GPS is leading me astray.

4469
04:42:00,370 --> 04:42:01,250
It's right here.

4470
04:42:05,830 --> 04:42:07,410
Man, look at the driving skills.

4471
04:42:11,110 --> 04:42:11,890
Oh, shit!

4472
04:42:15,950 --> 04:42:16,710
My bad.

4473
04:42:17,010 --> 04:42:17,290
Sorry.

4474
04:42:17,970 --> 04:42:18,730
Oh, no.

4475
04:42:18,850 --> 04:42:20,110
Look at the scratches, man.

4476
04:42:20,190 --> 04:42:21,490
I just had it repaired.

4477
04:42:22,630 --> 04:42:23,130
Fuck.

4478
04:42:28,680 --> 04:42:29,260
Damn.

4479
04:42:29,260 --> 04:42:30,320
Yeah, yeah.

4480
04:42:31,200 --> 04:42:32,060
Shut up.

4481
04:42:33,580 --> 04:42:34,880
Alright, let's go back here.

4482
04:42:37,160 --> 04:42:38,660
Why does this look like a kindergarten?

4483
04:42:48,180 --> 04:42:49,920
I keep getting different stories out of people.

4484
04:42:50,220 --> 04:42:55,920
One guy says the Majestic is... So you just listen to everyone's conversations, or...?

4485
04:42:55,920 --> 04:42:56,800
Would you relax?

4486
04:42:57,220 --> 04:42:59,200
Why the hell have you got it in for me?

4487
04:42:59,880 --> 04:43:00,840
Come over here and help me out!

4488
04:43:00,840 --> 04:43:01,620
Frank, where are you going?

4489
04:43:04,770 --> 04:43:05,950
The fuck's your problem?

4490
04:43:16,690 --> 04:43:22,970
What the fuck is this guy's problem?

4491
04:43:23,170 --> 04:43:24,030
What did I do to him?

4492
04:43:24,890 --> 04:43:26,870
I'm trying not to start shit here, you know?

4493
04:43:27,870 --> 04:43:29,890
I'm trying to keep it on the lowdown here.

4494
04:43:36,200 --> 04:43:38,460
Dude, I am so close to knocking this guy out.

4495
04:43:40,400 --> 04:43:40,880
What?

4496
04:43:52,640 --> 04:44:00,720
Sorry, I was just, you know... He was talking about eating something out of a stripper's ass and it would cost him 60k.

4497
04:44:02,860 --> 04:44:03,340
Cool.

4498
04:44:07,280 --> 04:44:08,720
Moonshine Boutique.

4499
04:44:13,640 --> 04:44:15,480
Wait, what am I supposed to do with contacts here?

4500
04:44:16,740 --> 04:44:18,340
Oh wait, Shirley sent us a message.

4501
04:44:19,880 --> 04:44:20,940
Thanks Han, my Ramos.

4502
04:44:21,220 --> 04:44:22,360
Oh yeah, we already did that one.

4503
04:44:23,700 --> 04:44:24,100
Done.

4504
04:44:26,640 --> 04:44:27,320
Reminders, maybe.

4505
04:44:28,840 --> 04:44:30,300
No, she posted again.

4506
04:44:32,420 --> 04:44:33,860
Oh, select contacts, I'm blind.

4507
04:44:36,840 --> 04:44:37,700
Let's see what he wants.

4508
04:44:38,780 --> 04:44:40,060
He's gonna give us some info on this.

4509
04:44:46,360 --> 04:44:48,320
Hey, so I'm at that boutique.

4510
04:44:48,460 --> 04:44:49,500
Yeah, boutique.

4511
04:44:49,720 --> 04:44:53,340
Ask those dorks how many wind chimes they sold since they moved in there.

4512
04:44:53,560 --> 04:44:54,580
It's an acid lab.

4513
04:44:54,800 --> 04:44:55,120
Okay.

4514
04:44:55,600 --> 04:44:56,840
So how do you want me to play this?

4515
04:44:57,000 --> 04:44:58,160
However you like.

4516
04:44:58,180 --> 04:45:01,100
I want my cut, and I want them out of there.

4517
04:45:01,340 --> 04:45:02,940
I covered them for long enough.

4518
04:45:05,040 --> 04:45:06,620
It's an acid lab?

4519
04:45:08,480 --> 04:45:11,140
To be honest, though, this whole place reminds me of Christiania.

4520
04:45:11,960 --> 04:45:15,340
A part of Copenhagen that is, like, a little self-sustaining.

4521
04:45:16,400 --> 04:45:19,760
And let's just say free in their ways.

4522
04:45:22,180 --> 04:45:23,120
Lab fees.

4523
04:45:25,520 --> 04:45:26,500
What's going on?

4524
04:45:43,480 --> 04:45:46,420
It's just a bullshit social construct anyways, my guy.

4525
04:45:46,620 --> 04:45:48,740
Point is, fuck Brian.

4526
04:45:48,980 --> 04:45:50,660
He ain't putting in the work like moi.

4527
04:45:52,420 --> 04:45:52,900
Huh.

4528
04:45:56,820 --> 04:45:58,280
Let's do this the easy way, bro.

4529
04:45:58,660 --> 04:46:00,160
Just give me Brian's rent and I'm gone.

4530
04:46:00,600 --> 04:46:01,780
Look, just think about it.

4531
04:46:01,860 --> 04:46:03,160
Does Brian really need the money?

4532
04:46:03,400 --> 04:46:04,160
Forget him.

4533
04:46:04,500 --> 04:46:05,600
That's how you wanna do it?

4534
04:46:06,160 --> 04:46:07,120
Yeah, I do.

4535
04:46:08,000 --> 04:46:09,340
Do something about it.

4536
04:46:14,380 --> 04:46:15,800
Whoa, hey!

4537
04:46:40,590 --> 04:46:41,750
0420, of course.

4538
04:46:44,070 --> 04:46:44,670
Dude...

4539
04:46:45,400 --> 04:46:47,220
I wish I could smash up his shop.

4540
04:46:48,200 --> 04:46:49,200
That's what I would do.

4541
04:46:49,680 --> 04:46:50,120
Restrained.

4542
04:46:51,880 --> 04:46:54,140
Wait, so these actions I have here actually do matter.

4543
04:46:55,420 --> 04:46:56,700
Look at all the detail.

4544
04:46:56,860 --> 04:46:58,060
How are they doing this?

4545
04:46:59,180 --> 04:47:00,280
This looks unreal.

4546
04:47:04,580 --> 04:47:05,020
Wow.

4547
04:47:06,300 --> 04:47:07,400
Let me see if I can actually...

4548
04:47:11,850 --> 04:47:12,470
Jason!

4549
04:47:13,650 --> 04:47:14,730
Are you stupid?

4550
04:47:16,530 --> 04:47:17,710
Toggle arc on?

4551
04:47:20,330 --> 04:47:21,230
Wait, arc?

4552
04:47:22,850 --> 04:47:24,370
Oh, for throwing, I guess.

4553
04:47:27,950 --> 04:47:28,390
Okay.

4554
04:47:29,010 --> 04:47:29,650
Just testing.

4555
04:47:31,490 --> 04:47:32,830
Alright, let's get back there.

4556
04:47:34,050 --> 04:47:35,110
Let's collect that shit.

4557
04:47:35,830 --> 04:47:36,630
0420, was it?

4558
04:47:38,390 --> 04:47:38,970
What's that?

4559
04:47:40,390 --> 04:47:44,310
List, glass beakers, burners, chips, tie-dye shirts, new bong.

4560
04:47:47,650 --> 04:47:48,090
0420.

4561
04:47:49,230 --> 04:47:52,270
Wait, so if I hadn't gotten the code from him, I could have gotten it here.

4562
04:47:54,810 --> 04:47:55,470
That's cool.

4563
04:48:02,880 --> 04:48:04,780
Kinda shitty security, I'll have to say.

4564
04:48:14,220 --> 04:48:14,720
Nice.

4565
04:48:16,180 --> 04:48:19,700
Am I gonna expect some company here, or...

4566
04:48:24,450 --> 04:48:24,950
Okay.

4567
04:48:25,530 --> 04:48:27,310
That looks sophisticated.

4568
04:48:29,930 --> 04:48:34,070
Stow bags and items in any vehicle trunk, including your personal vehicle, for easy transport.

4569
04:48:36,790 --> 04:48:37,290
Aha.

4570
04:48:43,190 --> 04:48:44,690
Oh, I just broke that like that.

4571
04:48:44,690 --> 04:48:44,950
Okay.

4572
04:48:51,080 --> 04:48:52,040
That's a lot of drugs.

4573
04:48:53,680 --> 04:48:55,660
I wonder if I can take the drugs and use them.

4574
04:48:56,300 --> 04:48:56,920
Probably not.

4575
04:48:59,380 --> 04:49:00,900
I mean, it is a GTA game.

4576
04:49:01,600 --> 04:49:02,260
Who knows.

4577
04:49:04,120 --> 04:49:04,560
Okay.

4578
04:49:05,120 --> 04:49:06,260
We got the good stuff.

4579
04:49:08,220 --> 04:49:09,080
Let's get out of here.

4580
04:49:11,740 --> 04:49:12,180
Brian!

4581
04:49:13,120 --> 04:49:14,100
I got your shit.

4582
04:49:25,030 --> 04:49:28,990
Well, he didn't have enough cash for his rent, but... I got some acid, though.

4583
04:49:29,650 --> 04:49:30,410
Will I cover your cut?

4584
04:49:30,630 --> 04:49:31,650
It'll do for now.

4585
04:49:32,090 --> 04:49:35,910
I gotta lock up next door at the Isla Tropicale private club.

4586
04:49:36,350 --> 04:49:39,290
Head inside, put whatever you got in the strong box.

4587
04:49:39,290 --> 04:49:41,730
I'll swing by later to see if we're square.

4588
04:49:42,030 --> 04:49:42,330
Cool.

4589
04:49:42,790 --> 04:49:43,750
Do I need a key or something?

4590
04:49:43,890 --> 04:49:44,630
Oh, right.

4591
04:49:44,630 --> 04:49:46,290
I forgot this was a Donnie job.

4592
04:49:46,570 --> 04:49:50,010
The code is 7700.

4593
04:49:50,790 --> 04:49:51,350
Got it.

4594
04:49:55,180 --> 04:49:55,700
Okay.

4595
04:49:55,700 --> 04:49:57,120
View nearby locations.

4596
04:49:58,040 --> 04:50:00,460
Select Brian's lockup?

4597
04:50:03,980 --> 04:50:04,500
Oh!

4598
04:50:05,860 --> 04:50:06,860
Oh, that's cool.

4599
04:50:07,320 --> 04:50:08,900
That's like a quick way to do it.

4600
04:50:09,540 --> 04:50:13,560
Brian will pay for any narcotics, jewelry, and marked bills dropped off at his lockup.

4601
04:50:20,340 --> 04:50:20,700
Done.

4602
04:50:20,700 --> 04:50:21,060
Okay.

4603
04:50:21,700 --> 04:50:23,040
I just want to take a look in here though.

4604
04:50:27,900 --> 04:50:30,800
Maybe I shouldn't be walking around with a bat in my hand.

4605
04:50:31,980 --> 04:50:33,120
Can I like stow that?

4606
04:50:40,390 --> 04:50:41,870
I guess I don't need to carry that around.

4607
04:50:42,570 --> 04:50:43,670
I don't want to scare her.

4608
04:50:45,030 --> 04:50:45,410
Hey!

4609
04:50:51,730 --> 04:50:53,850
Let me have a look around.

4610
04:50:56,330 --> 04:50:57,910
Now I know I can zoom in.

4611
04:51:01,260 --> 04:51:02,260
Wait, how does that work again?

4612
04:51:03,620 --> 04:51:05,220
No, don't, don't do that.

4613
04:51:05,920 --> 04:51:07,400
Yeah, sorry, I was trying to zoom.

4614
04:51:07,940 --> 04:51:08,620
You know how it is.

4615
04:51:08,840 --> 04:51:10,420
And then you accidentally pull out a gat.

4616
04:51:11,920 --> 04:51:12,540
Changing room.

4617
04:51:15,970 --> 04:51:18,430
I guess you can walk in here if you have cops on you.

4618
04:51:19,130 --> 04:51:22,210
Quickly change out the drip.

4619
04:51:24,350 --> 04:51:26,250
So wait, how do I actually zoom on command?

4620
04:51:26,830 --> 04:51:27,790
I need to figure this out.

4621
04:51:27,930 --> 04:51:29,170
So I hold this button.

4622
04:51:30,090 --> 04:51:36,790
Then I wait for an interaction prompt or... Do not pull the gun out, Jason.

4623
04:51:38,150 --> 04:51:39,390
I know you were in the army.

4624
04:51:39,630 --> 04:51:41,810
You don't have to, you know, tell everybody all the time.

4625
04:51:42,450 --> 04:51:42,870
Bracelets.

4626
04:51:45,040 --> 04:51:47,180
No way I get to wear bracelets too.

4627
04:51:48,280 --> 04:51:49,360
I mean, why not?

4628
04:51:50,540 --> 04:51:54,960
We can... I like that one.

4629
04:52:00,940 --> 04:52:01,460
Yep.

4630
04:52:01,460 --> 04:52:01,980
Thanks.

4631
04:52:03,040 --> 04:52:03,820
It's cool.

4632
04:52:05,080 --> 04:52:05,740
T-shirts.

4633
04:52:05,900 --> 04:52:06,260
What's this?

4634
04:52:07,940 --> 04:52:09,480
Bonbon tanning oil.

4635
04:52:09,760 --> 04:52:10,540
What even is that?

4636
04:52:10,820 --> 04:52:13,720
You put it on and you... Oh, wait.

4637
04:52:13,780 --> 04:52:14,860
It's like the fake tan.

4638
04:52:15,040 --> 04:52:16,100
You spray your tan on.

4639
04:52:16,480 --> 04:52:17,300
Never understood that.

4640
04:52:21,660 --> 04:52:26,600
I mean, that's just... I guess if you go swimming...

4641
04:52:29,520 --> 04:52:30,640
What's happening out there?

4642
04:52:32,880 --> 04:52:34,400
Flat-top aviators.

4643
04:52:37,120 --> 04:52:38,080
29 bucks.

4644
04:52:38,780 --> 04:52:39,460
You know what?

4645
04:52:39,580 --> 04:52:40,320
I'll take him.

4646
04:52:42,420 --> 04:52:43,840
That's Vice City right there.

4647
04:52:45,760 --> 04:52:46,900
Something about it, you know?

4648
04:52:47,560 --> 04:52:48,060
Thank you!

4649
04:53:08,500 --> 04:53:09,140
The potluck?

4650
04:53:11,100 --> 04:53:13,480
Ooh, I really want to steal this scooter.

4651
04:53:15,220 --> 04:53:17,780
Actually, I want to take it and put it in the trunk of my car.

4652
04:53:19,400 --> 04:53:20,700
I doubt I can do it, though.

4653
04:53:21,450 --> 04:53:22,650
But I would love to do it.

4654
04:53:23,390 --> 04:53:24,630
I can't leave my car behind.

4655
04:53:30,430 --> 04:53:32,830
Okay, so he puts the... in his car.

4656
04:53:39,610 --> 04:53:41,210
Did one of my lights go out in the back?

4657
04:53:42,590 --> 04:53:44,510
I think I broke one of my lights.

4658
04:53:46,430 --> 04:53:49,990
Yeah, look, the blinker is on in the front, but the backlight isn't working.

4659
04:53:52,130 --> 04:53:53,070
This side is working.

4660
04:53:54,890 --> 04:53:55,850
Dude, I love that.

4661
04:53:56,370 --> 04:53:57,110
Great detail.

4662
04:53:57,270 --> 04:53:58,510
We gotta get this shit repaired again.

4663
04:54:04,270 --> 04:54:07,690
Okay, let's just go straight there and drop off this thing, this asset.

4664
04:54:28,860 --> 04:54:30,140
That's the place right there.

4665
04:54:37,120 --> 04:54:37,680
Okay!

4666
04:54:39,880 --> 04:54:40,660
Sound good?

4667
04:54:45,620 --> 04:54:47,560
Dude, I'm drinking in these environments.

4668
04:54:48,060 --> 04:54:52,580
Like, everywhere I drive, I'm just, like, soaking it, you know, like a sponge.

4669
04:54:53,520 --> 04:54:56,760
And a bunch of good chemicals are being released in my brain.

4670
04:54:57,000 --> 04:54:57,660
Every time.

4671
04:54:59,460 --> 04:55:01,180
Graphics matter, if you do it right.

4672
04:55:02,940 --> 04:55:11,500
Obviously, gameplay is king, but you can't deny that in a game that's trying to simulate real life to an extent, graphics are important.

4673
04:55:12,260 --> 04:55:12,900
You know?

4674
04:55:14,890 --> 04:55:16,270
I fucking nailed it.

4675
04:55:19,570 --> 04:55:24,590
I need the bag and Brian Strongbox for him to collect later.

4676
04:55:25,470 --> 04:55:25,930
Sure.

4677
04:55:31,870 --> 04:55:32,690
Oh yeah.

4678
04:55:37,710 --> 04:55:39,630
Drop that stuff from the boutique.

4679
04:55:44,440 --> 04:55:49,480
I don't know if I'm a fan of that music, that little song that plays after a mission.

4680
04:55:50,480 --> 04:55:54,760
It's not quite iconic the same way, you know, San Andreas' music was, for example.

4681
04:55:55,820 --> 04:55:56,300
Thanks, son.

4682
04:55:56,560 --> 04:55:57,600
I'll check them when I can.

4683
04:55:57,740 --> 04:55:59,300
Got other business to take care of first.

4684
04:56:00,320 --> 04:56:01,220
Sounds good, Brian.

4685
04:56:02,800 --> 04:56:04,300
Got engines for boats here.

4686
04:56:04,960 --> 04:56:06,400
Bring stolen goods to drop-offs.

4687
04:56:06,500 --> 04:56:08,740
Like Brian's lock-up, you'll get paid after they're collected.

4688
04:56:09,740 --> 04:56:12,800
So wait, I can just, like, go around and steal stuff or what?

4689
04:56:15,350 --> 04:56:16,430
Hold on, let me sue him.

4690
04:56:16,950 --> 04:56:18,270
Oh, now I can inspect.

4691
04:56:18,610 --> 04:56:19,870
Maybe it's only indoors.

4692
04:56:23,590 --> 04:56:24,690
That's a nice poster.

4693
04:56:25,070 --> 04:56:26,330
That is very American.

4694
04:56:26,930 --> 04:56:29,770
She's got the American flag on her... boops.

4695
04:56:32,690 --> 04:56:34,710
Is she out there doing archery?

4696
04:56:34,870 --> 04:56:35,890
Bow hunting, maybe.

4697
04:56:41,430 --> 04:56:43,330
Also, I think I messed up the keybind.

4698
04:56:43,410 --> 04:56:45,390
Maybe you can zoom outside.

4699
04:56:46,290 --> 04:56:48,150
I forgot to click R3.

4700
04:56:48,410 --> 04:56:49,970
Instead, I tried to press R2.

4701
04:56:54,610 --> 04:56:55,810
Is that... hold on, is that weed?

4702
04:56:59,430 --> 04:57:00,830
Can I grab one of these real quick?

4703
04:57:01,210 --> 04:57:02,770
I see some of them are rolled already.

4704
04:57:06,260 --> 04:57:07,080
Probably wouldn't mind.

4705
04:57:07,900 --> 04:57:09,040
Okay, I can't click on that.

4706
04:57:09,840 --> 04:57:10,720
Alright, let's get out of here.

4707
04:57:11,760 --> 04:57:12,300
That's nice.

4708
04:57:27,010 --> 04:57:28,250
What are they doing over there?

4709
04:57:29,130 --> 04:57:29,930
Having a beer.

4710
04:57:30,370 --> 04:57:31,090
Should we go join them?

4711
04:57:32,890 --> 04:57:33,730
Let's go join them.

4712
04:57:35,910 --> 04:57:40,770
Just go over there and be like, hey, so I noticed in my binoculars that you guys were having a party.

4713
04:57:41,770 --> 04:57:43,110
And I had to join in.

4714
04:57:44,130 --> 04:57:47,610
That's such a creepy thing to say if you approach someone like that.

4715
04:57:49,790 --> 04:57:50,190
Hey!

4716
04:58:06,180 --> 04:58:06,700
Ha!

4717
04:58:06,960 --> 04:58:06,960
Ha!

4718
04:58:09,890 --> 04:58:10,710
What was that?

4719
04:58:19,830 --> 04:58:20,530
See ya.

4720
04:58:21,710 --> 04:58:22,250
Noops.

4721
04:58:23,930 --> 04:58:25,490
Are they actually following me?

4722
04:58:30,810 --> 04:58:32,330
They went back to their thing.

4723
04:58:33,950 --> 04:58:35,070
I'm a menace.

4724
04:58:47,590 --> 04:58:48,490
Oh shit!

4725
04:58:55,810 --> 04:58:56,710
Hey, Brian!

4726
04:58:57,590 --> 04:58:58,150
Jason!

4727
04:58:58,450 --> 04:58:58,850
What's up?

4728
04:58:59,270 --> 04:58:59,950
I need you.

4729
04:59:00,230 --> 04:59:02,250
I'm meeting Arnold, my contact.

4730
04:59:27,320 --> 04:59:27,760
Okay.

4731
04:59:27,760 --> 04:59:29,340
I mean, I got a piece.

4732
04:59:30,260 --> 04:59:31,540
In fact, I got a couple.

4733
04:59:33,140 --> 04:59:34,320
Let me see where that is.

4734
04:59:38,020 --> 04:59:38,720
Meet Brian.

4735
04:59:39,300 --> 04:59:41,620
Brian said to meet him at the Krastenberg Hotel.

4736
04:59:41,860 --> 04:59:42,920
Sounds like there's some trouble.

4737
04:59:44,520 --> 04:59:45,140
Sounds good.

4738
04:59:51,080 --> 04:59:52,840
Hold on, can I actually do a wheel spin or whatever?

4739
05:00:04,740 --> 05:00:07,540
I do wonder if I break my wheels if I do that too much.

4740
05:00:13,230 --> 05:00:15,910
Man, I love the AI on the road in this game.

4741
05:00:17,010 --> 05:00:22,930
They're actually behaving like, well, much more realistic drivers compared to other Grand Theft Autos.

4742
05:00:23,310 --> 05:00:24,970
They're not as annoying either, you know?

4743
05:00:26,070 --> 05:00:28,570
They don't randomly stop or do random shit.

4744
05:00:28,730 --> 05:00:29,670
They just drive.

4745
05:00:30,750 --> 05:00:32,810
Do their thing, and what's going on there?

4746
05:00:34,730 --> 05:00:36,030
Hold up, we gotta investigate.

4747
05:00:46,140 --> 05:00:47,580
Can I look through the window?

4748
05:00:48,620 --> 05:00:49,260
Oh shit.

4749
05:00:55,140 --> 05:00:56,820
How do I use this in the car?

4750
05:01:01,800 --> 05:01:04,120
What is wrong with these people in Leonida?

4751
05:01:13,960 --> 05:01:15,120
He got tasered.

4752
05:01:27,920 --> 05:01:29,300
Okay, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

4753
05:01:31,800 --> 05:01:34,320
I'm leaving, I'm leaving.

4754
05:01:50,630 --> 05:01:51,670
Craziest people here.

4755
05:01:52,710 --> 05:01:58,210
Maybe that's just what it's like over in the Oneida or... I'm assuming it's like Florida, right?

4756
05:01:58,670 --> 05:01:59,750
Because the Oneida man.

4757
05:02:02,110 --> 05:02:04,210
I wonder how true to life old is this?

4758
05:02:05,610 --> 05:02:07,590
Or if this is completely overdone, you know?

4759
05:02:15,170 --> 05:02:18,730
I can't get over how fucking realistic some of this lighting is.

4760
05:02:19,450 --> 05:02:22,210
Like, I constantly go like, wait a minute, that looks like a real picture.

4761
05:02:23,850 --> 05:02:24,790
From real life.

4762
05:02:33,110 --> 05:02:35,050
I would say my parking is decent.

4763
05:02:36,030 --> 05:02:39,250
You can manage your loadout in your trunk or any ammunition.

4764
05:02:39,510 --> 05:02:41,070
Oh yeah, right, he wanted us to bring a piece.

4765
05:02:43,980 --> 05:02:45,140
Let me see what I got here.

4766
05:02:46,500 --> 05:02:47,740
I mean, I have a pistol.

4767
05:02:47,940 --> 05:02:48,640
That'll be fine, right?

4768
05:02:48,880 --> 05:02:49,420
Let's close this.

4769
05:02:52,020 --> 05:02:52,900
In fact, I have two.

4770
05:02:53,560 --> 05:02:55,020
I have a Scorpio Nipper.

4771
05:02:57,760 --> 05:02:58,780
Not as much damage.

4772
05:03:00,020 --> 05:03:00,940
This one is way better.

4773
05:03:02,920 --> 05:03:04,360
Okay, let's just keep this at the ready.

4774
05:03:07,240 --> 05:03:08,560
I think the entrance is over here.

4775
05:03:27,810 --> 05:03:29,490
Where are my binoculars?

4776
05:03:34,750 --> 05:03:39,470
Oh, shit.

4777
05:03:40,850 --> 05:03:42,570
They saw me peeking.

4778
05:03:45,570 --> 05:03:47,650
Krastenberg Hotel and Resorts.

4779
05:03:52,730 --> 05:03:54,470
Hey, Arnold!

4780
05:04:19,530 --> 05:04:27,790
Now, I don't often get stood up, but, uh, what the fuck else am I supposed to be assuming here, Jason?

4781
05:04:28,050 --> 05:04:29,170
We know where he's at.

4782
05:04:30,430 --> 05:04:32,490
Are you not fucking listening to me?

4783
05:04:32,550 --> 05:04:33,290
He's gone!

4784
05:04:33,510 --> 05:04:34,030
Dark!

4785
05:04:34,790 --> 05:04:36,450
Nah, shit, I'll find him.

4786
05:04:36,970 --> 05:04:37,830
Cal's on it.

4787
05:04:37,990 --> 05:04:40,030
I need you to drive so I can pick him up.

4788
05:04:41,130 --> 05:04:41,810
Where to?

4789
05:04:42,710 --> 05:04:43,530
Liquor store.

4790
05:04:43,730 --> 05:04:44,310
Where else?

4791
05:04:44,450 --> 05:04:45,150
Of course.

4792
05:04:45,370 --> 05:04:46,010
Of course.

4793
05:04:48,310 --> 05:04:49,290
I'll be taking a beer.

4794
05:04:49,870 --> 05:04:50,590
For the road!

4795
05:04:56,210 --> 05:04:57,610
Man, I love the drinking!

4796
05:05:02,690 --> 05:05:04,850
Maybe you shouldn't be drinking, then.

4797
05:05:05,950 --> 05:05:06,830
Yeah, fuck this.

4798
05:05:10,670 --> 05:05:12,150
Gotta stay sharp for this one, right?

4799
05:05:18,690 --> 05:05:20,650
Now this is a real American car.

4800
05:05:33,160 --> 05:05:35,560
Wait, so what is it they want me to do here all the time?

4801
05:05:36,300 --> 05:05:36,620
Cinematic?

4802
05:05:38,000 --> 05:05:38,320
Oh!

4803
05:05:44,240 --> 05:05:45,640
That's a little too scary to do.

4804
05:05:45,920 --> 05:05:46,880
Can I, like, not do that?

4805
05:05:50,940 --> 05:05:54,220
Oh god, stop.

4806
05:05:54,500 --> 05:05:55,460
There we go, now I can see.

4807
05:05:55,720 --> 05:05:57,060
How could you ever drive like that?

4808
05:05:59,280 --> 05:06:00,760
Maybe it thrives automatically.

4809
05:06:09,220 --> 05:06:10,540
Oh, you want to be over there.

4810
05:06:12,980 --> 05:06:13,980
You got it.

4811
05:06:24,240 --> 05:06:24,840
Kel!

4812
05:06:34,090 --> 05:06:35,550
All his beers broke.

4813
05:06:35,890 --> 05:06:36,610
Shit.

4814
05:06:44,700 --> 05:06:46,080
Looks like East Abysma?

4815
05:06:46,280 --> 05:06:46,460
No.

4816
05:06:47,240 --> 05:06:48,000
Maroon Key?

4817
05:06:48,580 --> 05:06:50,440
I guess that's the big aerostat thing.

4818
05:06:50,440 --> 05:06:52,000
You got some news for me, Cal?

4819
05:06:52,300 --> 05:07:02,500
So, yeah, assuming this guy's using the same number, and that number isn't registered to more than one phone or device, and that phone or device is still in his possession... Oh, enough.

4820
05:07:02,820 --> 05:07:04,020
Have we got him, Cal?

4821
05:07:04,160 --> 05:07:04,800
Yes or no?

4822
05:07:05,040 --> 05:07:05,580
I got him.

4823
05:07:05,640 --> 05:07:06,180
I got him.

4824
05:07:06,240 --> 05:07:07,260
Okay, that's where we flicked.

4825
05:07:08,120 --> 05:07:09,520
Oh, okay, you see right there?

4826
05:07:09,660 --> 05:07:11,100
That blimps the aerostat.

4827
05:07:16,090 --> 05:07:16,950
Oh yeah, I see it.

4828
05:08:05,830 --> 05:08:07,190
Okay... Wait, what did...

4829
05:08:07,480 --> 05:08:08,540
What the hell?

4830
05:08:10,760 --> 05:08:11,780
That looks so good.

4831
05:08:12,040 --> 05:08:13,460
I want to get up in that blimp.

4832
05:08:21,500 --> 05:08:23,360
Oh, good, your phone is working.

4833
05:08:23,360 --> 05:08:26,280
I just... I just wanted to check that out.

4834
05:08:26,860 --> 05:08:30,860
So, are you just trying to, uh, ghost me?

4835
05:08:31,160 --> 05:08:31,680
Or what?

4836
05:08:31,900 --> 05:08:33,020
There's a system, okay?

4837
05:08:33,100 --> 05:08:34,000
And you almost fucked it.

4838
05:08:34,300 --> 05:08:37,640
Word got around that you're not dependable, you and your cabin boys.

4839
05:08:37,880 --> 05:08:39,520
But you get these guys, man.

4840
05:08:39,680 --> 05:08:40,560
I mean, look at them.

4841
05:08:41,280 --> 05:08:44,340
I bring you in, and then what, you start a turf war?

4842
05:08:44,620 --> 05:08:49,760
I mean, how does a guy like you, Brian, get the fucking nerve or the balls?

4843
05:08:50,170 --> 05:08:51,870
Let me make something perfectly clear.

4844
05:08:52,070 --> 05:08:53,890
We didn't start it.

4845
05:08:54,030 --> 05:08:54,930
We ended it.

4846
05:08:55,030 --> 05:08:56,470
And I'm coming to you as a courtesy.

4847
05:08:56,710 --> 05:08:57,570
Oh, my God.

4848
05:08:57,790 --> 05:09:02,830
No one gives a shit about your lousy 40, 50 kilos.

4849
05:09:03,110 --> 05:09:06,590
I mean, they are moving tons on the fucking cargo ships.

4850
05:09:06,750 --> 05:09:07,430
I've seen it.

4851
05:09:07,530 --> 05:09:12,410
Yeah, and I would bet that the vendors you're still working for would hate any further delays to their system.

4852
05:09:12,590 --> 05:09:13,490
So, what's it gonna be?

4853
05:09:13,530 --> 05:09:14,130
You and me?

4854
05:09:14,270 --> 05:09:17,250
We work something out, like men, or... Or what?

4855
05:09:17,980 --> 05:09:19,840
You gonna ask to speak to my manager?

4856
05:09:24,120 --> 05:09:27,600
Get me another line of distribution, Arnold.

4857
05:09:50,700 --> 05:09:52,100
Yeah!

4858
05:09:53,560 --> 05:09:54,960
Yes!

4859
05:09:55,780 --> 05:09:57,180
Yes!

4860
05:09:59,830 --> 05:10:01,610
Dude, the acting is so good.

4861
05:10:03,710 --> 05:10:09,090
Oh, cool.

4862
05:10:12,110 --> 05:10:13,730
Should I be trying to shoot him while driving?

4863
05:10:18,350 --> 05:10:20,190
Oh man, this car is hard to drive.

4864
05:10:26,590 --> 05:10:27,970
Use R1 to fire, okay.

4865
05:10:38,990 --> 05:10:41,130
Oh, man, this is so good!

4866
05:10:43,950 --> 05:10:45,550
Oh, yeah!

4867
05:10:46,690 --> 05:10:47,770
That was sweet!

4868
05:10:50,290 --> 05:10:51,730
Can we shoot the wheels, maybe?

4869
05:10:56,090 --> 05:10:56,890
Uh-oh.

4870
05:11:09,160 --> 05:11:09,540
Dale.

4871
05:11:14,080 --> 05:11:15,780
Oh, we got people on bikes now too.

4872
05:11:23,000 --> 05:11:24,100
My aim is terrible.

4873
05:11:24,300 --> 05:11:25,920
Maybe I'll just hit him with the car, man.

4874
05:11:26,180 --> 05:11:26,840
There we go.

4875
05:11:40,730 --> 05:11:41,830
I'm trying.

4876
05:11:45,830 --> 05:11:47,190
Jesus fuck.

4877
05:11:52,990 --> 05:12:05,010
Oh man, this thing turns like a bastard.

4878
05:12:11,180 --> 05:12:14,180
I love how you're actually inaccurate while driving, you know?

4879
05:12:14,240 --> 05:12:15,220
Haha, he crashed.

4880
05:12:28,840 --> 05:12:29,700
Ghost driver.

4881
05:12:38,360 --> 05:12:39,760
Yeah!

4882
05:12:47,360 --> 05:12:51,020
The pink glasses!

4883
05:12:52,620 --> 05:12:54,000
Okay, bro.

4884
05:13:00,950 --> 05:13:01,750
Come here, bro.

4885
05:13:04,570 --> 05:13:05,430
You know what I need?

4886
05:13:05,550 --> 05:13:08,130
I need a... cowboy rope right now.

4887
05:13:12,330 --> 05:13:13,390
I'm gonna tackle him.

4888
05:13:14,390 --> 05:13:15,650
Oh, I'm running out of stamina here.

4889
05:13:18,830 --> 05:13:19,750
Ah, come on.

4890
05:13:20,210 --> 05:13:20,910
Okay, you know what?

4891
05:13:23,050 --> 05:13:26,410
Can I, like... Ah.

4892
05:13:28,550 --> 05:13:28,950
Shit.

4893
05:13:32,910 --> 05:13:35,450
Is he planning to... No way, he's getting away.

4894
05:13:40,110 --> 05:13:41,290
Nowhere to go now, brother.

4895
05:14:33,300 --> 05:14:34,780
Right, really?

4896
05:14:43,480 --> 05:14:46,160
I don't think Brian's gonna like that very much.

4897
05:14:46,800 --> 05:14:47,580
But fuck him.

4898
05:14:49,180 --> 05:14:50,100
I'm not a killer.

4899
05:14:50,620 --> 05:14:53,620
I mean, except for those three punks outside the liquor store.

4900
05:15:03,410 --> 05:15:05,470
Laurie, let me talk to him for two seconds first.

4901
05:15:05,590 --> 05:15:06,450
All right, lovebug?

4902
05:15:06,730 --> 05:15:07,150
Come on.

4903
05:15:08,930 --> 05:15:12,070
So... You take care of that thing?

4904
05:15:12,550 --> 05:15:12,870
Here.

4905
05:15:13,830 --> 05:15:15,070
Arnold's gonna keep his mouth shut.

4906
05:15:16,310 --> 05:15:17,710
That's what I like to hear.

4907
05:15:18,530 --> 05:15:19,630
All right, that is done.

4908
05:15:20,130 --> 05:15:21,970
It is time to relax.

4909
05:15:22,830 --> 05:15:23,270
Great.

4910
05:15:23,550 --> 05:15:25,330
I can finally take these then.

4911
05:15:26,030 --> 05:15:28,250
I've been waiting to see unicorns, baby.

4912
05:15:28,610 --> 05:15:30,310
Yeah, Jason, come on over here.

4913
05:15:30,450 --> 05:15:31,530
I want you to meet my friend.

4914
05:15:38,780 --> 05:15:41,360
Man, this looks so good.

4915
05:15:59,590 --> 05:16:00,550
Treasure hunter.

4916
05:16:01,050 --> 05:16:01,990
Ain't that something?

4917
05:16:02,570 --> 05:16:05,170
It would be if I could still do it.

4918
05:16:05,850 --> 05:16:07,610
Fucking can't stuck my permit.

4919
05:16:07,770 --> 05:16:09,330
That is bullshit, dude.

4920
05:16:10,150 --> 05:16:11,530
Can't you just play dumb?

4921
05:16:11,810 --> 05:16:12,910
That's what I would do.

4922
05:16:13,610 --> 05:16:15,570
It's too late for me to do that, Cal.

4923
05:16:16,190 --> 05:16:17,150
But you're right, huh?

4924
05:16:17,630 --> 05:16:21,350
In these moments, you just gotta get very innovative, you know?

4925
05:16:21,910 --> 05:16:23,350
Find a new way.

4926
05:16:24,030 --> 05:16:24,450
Dip!

4927
05:16:24,710 --> 05:16:25,130
No!

4928
05:16:25,690 --> 05:16:26,710
No, dip!

4929
05:16:29,570 --> 05:16:30,870
Oh, what the hell?

4930
05:16:32,920 --> 05:16:33,060
What do you think?

4931
05:16:33,640 --> 05:16:34,740
Mushroom's good for him.

4932
05:16:36,960 --> 05:16:38,840
Jason, you can dive, can't you?

4933
05:16:39,320 --> 05:16:39,940
A little bit.

4934
05:16:40,360 --> 05:16:44,840
Treasure hunting is way more exciting than a little swim with the fish, my friend.

4935
05:16:45,820 --> 05:16:58,380
When you find something that's hundreds of years old, way out in the middle of the ocean, and you're holding it in your hands, suddenly you realize just how rich you're gonna be.

4936
05:17:00,480 --> 05:17:01,780
Yeah, but anyways...

4937
05:17:12,090 --> 05:17:14,170
Those drinks look so good.

4938
05:17:14,270 --> 05:17:14,650
Look at that.

4939
05:17:16,610 --> 05:17:18,350
I would love to do some treasure hunting.

4940
05:17:21,870 --> 05:17:26,950
Cal and, you know, the whole finding treasure stuff reminds me of Sahara.

4941
05:17:27,290 --> 05:17:28,150
That movie.

4942
05:17:28,990 --> 05:17:30,270
Something about that character.

4943
05:17:34,220 --> 05:17:35,280
Okay, okay, okay.

4944
05:17:36,540 --> 05:17:37,260
Let me see.

4945
05:17:39,460 --> 05:17:39,900
Bombora.

4946
05:17:40,060 --> 05:17:41,100
Okay, so that's my boat.

4947
05:17:43,000 --> 05:17:44,620
Map is updated with KR.

4948
05:17:46,260 --> 05:17:50,900
Recover owned long arms and manage your loadout from your trunk or an ammunition.

4949
05:17:51,100 --> 05:17:51,580
Yeah, I know that.

4950
05:17:53,120 --> 05:17:54,140
Work for Kenton.

4951
05:17:54,360 --> 05:17:55,440
Okay, so that was his name.

4952
05:17:55,900 --> 05:17:58,380
The treasure hunter you met at Brian's has work available.

4953
05:17:58,900 --> 05:18:00,340
Drop by his place in Key Lento.

4954
05:18:01,290 --> 05:18:03,170
Ooh, we get to dive or something, probably.

4955
05:18:04,450 --> 05:18:04,810
Brian?

4956
05:18:05,710 --> 05:18:06,410
One more thing.

4957
05:18:06,610 --> 05:18:09,730
Left your pay for those packages and that Mandy and Arnold business in your mailbox.

4958
05:18:10,130 --> 05:18:11,270
Let me know how it goes with Kenny.

4959
05:18:12,710 --> 05:18:13,210
Will do.

4960
05:18:18,290 --> 05:18:18,750
Oh, wait.

4961
05:18:19,010 --> 05:18:20,010
We have more conversations.

4962
05:18:22,970 --> 05:18:23,890
Do me a favor, kid.

4963
05:18:23,990 --> 05:18:25,030
Can you swing by Kenny's?

4964
05:18:25,090 --> 05:18:25,470
Help him out?

4965
05:18:26,150 --> 05:18:26,410
Right.

4966
05:18:27,490 --> 05:18:28,450
That's why we're there.

4967
05:18:28,790 --> 05:18:29,790
Or where we're going.

4968
05:18:30,630 --> 05:18:31,050
Kenton, right?

4969
05:18:31,210 --> 05:18:31,810
From the hot tub?

4970
05:18:31,970 --> 05:18:32,510
Yeah, I got you.

4971
05:18:32,710 --> 05:18:33,510
Thanks again for the drinks.

4972
05:18:33,610 --> 05:18:33,970
How's Dip?

4973
05:18:34,610 --> 05:18:36,110
I love these names for the animals.

4974
05:18:36,250 --> 05:18:37,570
Dip and Arugula.

4975
05:18:38,930 --> 05:18:39,490
He's fine.

4976
05:18:39,570 --> 05:18:41,050
Little shit's got a stomach like a gator.

4977
05:18:41,330 --> 05:18:42,110
It's extra in the morning, son.

4978
05:18:42,970 --> 05:18:43,330
Beautiful.

4979
05:18:44,250 --> 05:18:44,610
Okay.

4980
05:18:45,210 --> 05:18:47,170
So did we just work out, or was it just fake?

4981
05:18:47,390 --> 05:18:49,030
Oh, it was fake workout.

4982
05:18:49,590 --> 05:18:51,150
It didn't actually work out.

4983
05:18:53,050 --> 05:18:53,490
Okay.

4984
05:18:54,430 --> 05:18:55,790
Maybe it's time to read that magazine.

4985
05:18:56,210 --> 05:18:58,590
First, though, I'm gonna save the game.

4986
05:18:59,510 --> 05:19:00,810
And I'm gonna take a little break.

4987
05:19:04,530 --> 05:19:06,230
Maybe I should overwrite one of these.

4988
05:19:06,430 --> 05:19:06,710
No, no, no.

4989
05:19:06,810 --> 05:19:08,270
Just keep going.

4990
05:19:09,890 --> 05:19:10,290
Yeah.

4991
05:19:10,850 --> 05:19:12,150
Dude, this game is so much fun.

4992
05:19:12,890 --> 05:19:14,570
I am freaking loving this so far.

4993
05:19:15,730 --> 05:19:18,750
This is everything I wanted the game to be so far, at least.

4994
05:19:19,850 --> 05:19:20,330
Hey, look.

4995
05:19:20,390 --> 05:19:21,210
There's also stuff up there.

4996
05:19:21,690 --> 05:19:22,830
I didn't even see that earlier.

4997
05:19:24,070 --> 05:19:26,550
Like a little... What is that?

4998
05:19:28,750 --> 05:19:29,150
Swordfish.

4999
05:19:30,810 --> 05:19:31,430
Or something.

5000
05:19:31,730 --> 05:19:32,290
I don't know.

5001
05:19:32,960 --> 05:19:35,160
I will see you guys in like 10 minutes.

5002
05:19:35,320 --> 05:19:41,880
I'm gonna grab a little bit to eat and fill up my drink and go cuddle with my cat just slightly.

5003
05:19:42,080 --> 05:19:42,320
Be right back.

5004
05:27:05,740 --> 05:27:09,020
Guys, heating the food took a little longer than expected.

5005
05:27:09,020 --> 05:27:10,860
Give me like 10 more minutes or so.

5006
05:27:11,680 --> 05:27:13,740
I'm gonna put 10 extra minutes on it.

5007
05:27:14,060 --> 05:27:14,860
I'll be back soon.

5008
05:37:14,740 --> 05:37:15,740
Hey, what's up?

5009
05:37:18,520 --> 05:37:19,580
How's it going, guys?

5010
05:37:20,720 --> 05:37:22,200
What do you think of the game so far?

5011
05:37:24,060 --> 05:37:25,300
From what you've seen here?

5012
05:37:26,200 --> 05:37:29,420
Because I gotta tell you, man, I... I am blown away.

5013
05:37:30,320 --> 05:37:32,540
I already had high expectations for this.

5014
05:37:33,960 --> 05:37:36,000
And... It's so funny.

5015
05:37:36,280 --> 05:37:38,360
You know, like, the humor is on point.

5016
05:37:39,860 --> 05:37:43,420
Like, of course, the 30 FPS is kind of a bummer, but you know what?

5017
05:37:43,480 --> 05:37:44,460
I got used to it now.

5018
05:37:44,620 --> 05:37:46,220
So it's actually less of a bummer now.

5019
05:37:47,180 --> 05:37:52,720
But, you know, the trade-off to get those graphics and that fidelity, I will say, man, I don't mind it.

5020
05:37:52,880 --> 05:37:53,580
I really don't.

5021
05:37:54,960 --> 05:37:56,260
This slaps.

5022
05:37:57,500 --> 05:37:58,400
It slaps, man.

5023
05:37:59,500 --> 05:38:01,140
And it feels good to play as well.

5024
05:38:02,500 --> 05:38:06,260
Like the car handling and the way the weapons feel and stuff.

5025
05:38:06,420 --> 05:38:07,100
Very nice.

5026
05:38:11,060 --> 05:38:14,600
Okay, so I've noticed that... I think it's only on my end, though.

5027
05:38:15,800 --> 05:38:22,480
But... when I... I'm just switching between settings in the menu right now.

5028
05:38:23,620 --> 05:38:26,600
But... I felt like there was a bit of an audio delay.

5029
05:38:26,920 --> 05:38:28,860
But I can understand that it's not on your end.

5030
05:38:29,400 --> 05:38:32,400
So I tried to change the audio output just now.

5031
05:38:32,640 --> 05:38:35,880
So instead of, you know, listening or monitoring to...

5032
05:38:36,190 --> 05:38:38,090
We're monitoring the capture card.

5033
05:38:38,270 --> 05:38:46,570
I'm just directly plugged into my actual display, because audio is being transmitted via HDMI from the capture card.

5034
05:38:47,370 --> 05:38:48,730
So hopefully that will fix that.

5035
05:38:49,050 --> 05:38:52,010
But for you guys, you haven't noticed any audio delay at all, or what?

5036
05:38:52,590 --> 05:38:56,730
Because it was quite noticeable for me, like, the longer I play, the more audio delay.

5037
05:38:56,830 --> 05:38:59,470
Like, it's nothing crazy, but, you know, enough to be a little annoying.

5038
05:39:00,290 --> 05:39:02,330
So I don't know if you guys noticed anything like that.

5039
05:39:04,240 --> 05:39:06,960
I think it's just on my end that I had it, but it should be fixed now.

5040
05:39:08,300 --> 05:39:10,420
Your volume is a bit loud compared to the game too.

5041
05:39:10,600 --> 05:39:11,860
Okay, I can turn up the game slightly.

5042
05:39:15,460 --> 05:39:17,560
I can turn my voice down also slightly.

5043
05:39:19,000 --> 05:39:19,360
There.

5044
05:39:19,900 --> 05:39:23,480
Relative difference of two decibels now between these two.

5045
05:39:26,920 --> 05:39:27,780
You didn't notice it.

5046
05:39:27,860 --> 05:39:28,020
Okay.

5047
05:39:28,740 --> 05:39:30,140
I think it was just on my end then.

5048
05:39:31,360 --> 05:39:32,640
But that should be fixed now.

5049
05:39:43,270 --> 05:39:47,350
I already did do a bit of research beforehand, MaxRent.

5050
05:39:47,470 --> 05:39:51,990
Like, if you have licensed music in the game, you're just gonna get copyrights flagged on YouTube.

5051
05:39:54,770 --> 05:39:57,910
You are not gonna get any money for the video at all when you upload.

5052
05:39:58,110 --> 05:40:01,170
And worst case, you cannot even display the video in certain countries.

5053
05:40:01,310 --> 05:40:04,970
And worst case, you cannot put the video in public.

5054
05:40:07,330 --> 05:40:10,450
I guess I could put my own music, but that's also kind of weird, isn't it?

5055
05:40:13,630 --> 05:40:14,430
I guess I could.

5056
05:40:18,990 --> 05:40:21,610
We found out we can make shadow people on the wall with the start screen.

5057
05:40:21,830 --> 05:40:25,430
Yeah, the idea was for it to be like a shadow on the wall from the sun.

5058
05:40:26,550 --> 05:40:27,970
I don't know if it works that well, though.

5059
05:40:28,310 --> 05:40:30,010
Some of the emojis are just sort of squares.

5060
05:40:34,080 --> 05:40:35,620
Feels a little empty with no music.

5061
05:40:35,780 --> 05:40:43,340
Yeah, I mean... I feel like Rockstar could have put in at least some... I don't want to call it shitty, but some music... instead of just nothing.

5062
05:40:43,600 --> 05:40:44,820
This is a crazy decision.

5063
05:40:45,620 --> 05:40:46,120
You know?

5064
05:40:52,520 --> 05:40:53,400
No, we're not ending.

5065
05:40:53,520 --> 05:40:54,140
We're playing more.

5066
05:40:58,270 --> 05:41:03,390
Although I'm trying to see if I can... Nah, that's fine.

5067
05:41:07,670 --> 05:41:08,110
Okay.

5068
05:41:09,290 --> 05:41:10,290
Let's just get into it.

5069
05:41:14,470 --> 05:41:15,190
There we go.

5070
05:41:15,650 --> 05:41:17,130
Let's see what this store thing is.

5071
05:41:20,850 --> 05:41:21,630
Oh, God.

5072
05:41:23,570 --> 05:41:25,470
I guess we do live in 2026, huh?

5073
05:41:26,370 --> 05:41:27,730
We can't avoid that nowadays.

5074
05:41:30,670 --> 05:41:31,070
Okay.

5075
05:41:33,430 --> 05:41:35,690
Now... What's next?

5076
05:41:36,990 --> 05:41:37,590
You know what?

5077
05:41:37,590 --> 05:41:38,370
Let's do some reading.

5078
05:41:38,670 --> 05:41:40,810
I want to do... No, you know what?

5079
05:41:40,830 --> 05:41:41,430
Actually... No, no, no.

5080
05:41:41,830 --> 05:41:45,010
I feel like I'm going a little slow here in the beginning.

5081
05:41:45,010 --> 05:41:45,750
But that's okay.

5082
05:41:46,550 --> 05:41:48,950
Who's doing gardening at this time of the...

5083
05:41:49,630 --> 05:41:50,110
Morning.

5084
05:41:50,630 --> 05:41:53,170
Oh, it sounded like someone was chopping grass.

5085
05:41:56,010 --> 05:41:57,090
Let me get a look at that.

5086
05:41:59,650 --> 05:42:01,290
People love the jet skis, huh?

5087
05:42:07,860 --> 05:42:08,640
Oh, man.

5088
05:42:09,520 --> 05:42:10,860
This home is so good.

5089
05:42:12,320 --> 05:42:13,380
Let's close that up.

5090
05:42:14,740 --> 05:42:16,300
Did I get my morning coffee yet?

5091
05:42:17,800 --> 05:42:18,720
Not sure if I did.

5092
05:42:18,840 --> 05:42:19,600
What is the time, anyway?

5093
05:42:21,280 --> 05:42:22,080
10.23.

5094
05:42:22,400 --> 05:42:22,760
Okay.

